    "body": "So for example: something like ARWEAVEP captured, grabs raw the string.\r\nLike this: var decrypted = CryptoJS.AES.decrypt(ciphertext, userInput);\r\nwhich becomes the AES password,\r\n\r\nlike this: var key = CryptoJS.PBKDF2(userInput, salt, { keySize: 256/32,\r\niterations: 1000 });\r\nvar decrypted = CryptoJS.AES.decrypt(ciphertext, key, { iv: iv }); then AES\r\ndecrypt?\r\n\r\n\r\nOn Tue, May 6, 2025 at 5:50 PM Antony Cooper ***@***.***>\r\nwrote:\r\n\r\n> *HomelessPhD* left a comment (HomelessPhD/AR_Puzzles#11)\r\n> <https://github.com/HomelessPhD/AR_Puzzles/issues/11#issuecomment-2856167056>\r\n>\r\n> read carefully and try to follow it in the original code (or snippet i\r\n> given on the git page) - HOW the original puzzle page work with typed\r\n> solution -> how it process it before using as AES \"password\"\r\n>\r\n> —\r\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\r\n> <https://github.com/HomelessPhD/AR_Puzzles/issues/11#issuecomment-2856167056>,\r\n> or unsubscribe\r\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/BP6QMA6IGMB3HVLNWJYICNT25EVC3AVCNFSM6AAAAAB4RNOJHGVHI2DSMVQWIX3LMV43OSLTON2WKQ3PNVWWK3TUHMZDQNJWGE3DOMBVGY>\r\n> .\r\n> You are receiving this because you authored the thread.Message ID:\r\n> ***@***.***>\r\n>\r\n",
